course: dictionary
lesson: 15628
title: Televise: showing it on TV
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To televise something is to show it on television. Often it is shown live, which means people at home see it at the same time as it happens. «The cup final will be televised live tonight» tells you that you can watch the match on TV as it is played.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. Televise starts with «tele», which is the start of television, so the word is about TV. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence: «The Olympic opening ceremony was televised around the world» still makes sense if you think of it as shown on TV.
explain: The ending changes with time. «Televise» is what you do now, «televised» is what happened before, and «televising» is what is happening now. «The election results are being televised» means the TV is showing them at this moment.
fact: To televise means to show something on television.
fact: «Televised» is the past form: «The election was televised last night.»
fact: Things are often televised live, so people see them as they happen.
fact: Big football matches, royal events and the Olympics are often televised.
fact: Parliament debates are sometimes televised, so people can watch what their representatives do.
exercise: «The cup final will be televised live.» What does televised mean here? | *Shown on television | Written down in a newspaper | Played in an empty stadium | Cancelled because of rain
exercise: «The Olympic opening ceremony was televised around the world.» Find and copy the word that means shown on TV. | *televised | ceremony | world | Olympic
exercise: Parliament debates are sometimes televised. Why might that be? | To make the debate shorter | *So people can watch what their representatives do | So the members can sleep in peace | To stop people going to the park
test: «The election results were televised late at night.» What does televised mean? | Hidden from view | *Shown on television | Printed on paper | Shouted through a loudspeaker
test: «The school play was not televised.» What does this tell you? | *It was not shown on television | It was played in the rain | It was shown live on television | It was watched by the whole school
exam: Why might a football game's start time be changed so it can be televised? | So the crowd can arrive late | *So that more people at home can watch it live | So the referee can go home early | So the players can have a longer rest
